			<div class="content" id="post-content-3695406">
									

<p>The article doesn't state anywhere what SCP-3129's area of effect actually is. Is it just the continental United States? Has it appeared anywhere else outside the United States? Does SCP-3129 appear more often in places where the ideas of community and togetherness are &quot;on the decline&quot;? Or does it prefer places where those ideas are already strongly valued? How frequent are SCP-3129 infected broadcasts?</p>
<p>The description lead me to believe that SCP-3129-1 has specific ideas that people who already agree with make them more susceptible to infection, but the example log at the bottom seems to cite 3129-1's main ideas as security, togetherness, and community which are pretty board and popular ideas among any stock politician regardless of party, and ideas which include a pretty broad amount of potentially vulnerable infectees. Wouldn't that pool of possible cognitohazard-vectors as well as the incident report (which might suggest possible reality reconstruction or at least a perception-based effect) be a point of concern for the Foundation to at least consider a pending Keter classification?</p>
<p>I don't wanna downvote, but I just feel like the ideas as they are presented here aren't fully developed and realized. If can address a few of these questions in some edits, I think I could confidently upvote this. Otherwise, this feels like it's almost something good but just not quite there yet.</p>

							</div>

								
					
